/// Plain-language duty descriptions for slice 3 of the MOS roster.
///
/// WRITTEN BY HAND, ONE LINE AT A TIME, FROM THE CITED PAGE. Not generated by a
/// script: every sentence below was written in this repo's own words after
/// reading the source named on the entry, which is the only way a description
/// field can be filled without becoming a guess.
///
/// ## What belongs in this file
///
/// Slice 3 is indices 78..116 (inclusive) of the 156 MOS codes in the roster,
/// sorted alphabetically: 39 codes, from 40D to 88L. The slice exists so the
/// description pass divides without overlap; codes the other slices carry are
/// simply absent here, and an absent entry is not a claim about anything.
///
/// Each entry is two sentences: what the work actually is, and where it is
/// trained or performed. Nothing here repeats a sentence from the source - the
/// text is a paraphrase, and the source URL travels with it so the paraphrase
/// can be checked against the original rather than trusted.
///
/// ## Where the text comes from
///
/// 38 of the 39 entries are paraphrased from the "Major duties" paragraph and
/// the mandatory-training qualification of that MOS's own section in DA Pam
/// 611-21, chapter 10, section C (Enlisted MOS specifications), 04 December 2025
/// build - the same authority the roster's gates are transcribed from. That
/// build is published as one chapter file, so [pamphletUrl] is the citation the
/// text is checked against; the per-MOS section reference is already carried by
/// Mos.source in lib/data/repos/mos_data.dart.
///
/// 42S is the exception: that chapter file carries no 42S section, so its
/// description is paraphrased from the U.S. Army's own short summary of the job
/// on its recruiting site ([specialBandSummaryUrl]), which names the four
/// special bands a special band musician serves in.
///
/// ## What this file does NOT claim
///
/// Two sentences cannot carry everything the pamphlet says, and a description is
/// not a qualification: the gate, the physical demand and the clearance still
/// come from the roster entries and are confirmed by a recruiter. Text here is
/// shown only alongside its citation - a description that cannot show its source
/// is not shown at all.
library;

import '../models/mos.dart';

/// The day the pages cited here were read, as a date rather than a timestamp.
final DateTime mosDescriptionSlice3RetrievedOn = DateTime(2026, 10, 26);

/// DA Pam 611-21, chapter 10, section C: the enlisted MOS specifications.
const String pamphletUrl =
    'https://api.army.mil/e2/c/downloads/2025/12/04/20612de5/'
    'chapter-10c-enlisted-mos-specifications.pdf';

/// The U.S. Army's short official summary of what a 42S does.
const String specialBandSummaryUrl =
    'https://www.goarmy.com/careers-and-jobs/support-logistics/creative/'
    '42s-special-band-musician';

/// Codes in slice 3 that were left out, with the reason recorded in the slice
/// report instead of invented into a sentence.
///
/// Empty: every code in this slice could be described from a page that was
/// actually read.
const List<String> mosDescriptionSlice3Omitted = <String>[];

/// The 39 descriptions, keyed by MOS code, in code order.
///
/// `final` rather than `const` only because [SourcedText] carries a [DateTime],
/// which has no const constructor; the map itself is never mutated.
final Map<String, SourcedText> mosDescriptionSlice3 = <String, SourcedText>{
  '40D': _describe(
